maluos-office-setup (0.1.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Application servers (MaluOS Phase 14 slice 3).
    scripts/application-server.py: --show, --check the kernel's
    applications' door and say which side to fix, --apply writes role:
    application-server, the application_server block and the estate
    enrolment into firstboot.yaml (the join code from a file).
    configure-kernel.py --application-servers sets the kernel's list of
    admitted servers. proxy-config.sh gives an application on a server of
    its own that server as its upstream (maluctl app names --upstreams).
  * references/application-server.md: the three kinds of server, the order
    they are set up in, what each interview asks; the skill follows it.
  * maluctl office-setup application-server.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

maluos-office-setup (0.1.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * /office-website: the public page at the bare name. The skill turns the
    starter page of first boot (Bootstrap 5.3 and htmx, static files) into
    the business's own on a working copy in the operator's home, shows what
    will go live and publishes on their word; references/bootstrap-htmx.md
    is the house style for the markup.
  * scripts/landing-site.sh, the one privileged step: status, checkout DIR,
    publish DIR (refuses symlinks, dot files, server-side code, a missing
    index.html; backs the live page up, replaces it whole), restore.
  * maluctl office-setup website [status|checkout|publish|restore].
  * Where the data lives (MaluOS Phase 14). The interview asks (Phase 1b):
    this server's own PostgreSQL, or a MaluOS database server. For a
    database server, scripts/database-server.py --check connects as the
    admin role over TLS with the certificate verified and says which side
    to fix when it cannot; --apply writes the database_server block of
    firstboot.yaml (nothing is moved; refused on a kernel already
    provisioned locally without --data-not-moved). preflight.py and
    verify.sh report where the data is and that it answers;
    references/database-server.md says what is supported: one kernel
    server per database server, no separate application servers yet.
    maluctl office-setup database.
  * plugin.json says the package's version.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000

maluos-office-setup (0.1.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The sign-in name is said plainly. The owner's first sign-in was refused
    with a correct password because another email was typed (the office was
    on https the whole time; the http cookie fault of 0.1.1 was real but not
    that failure). The skill writes the administrator's email out in full at
    the hand-off and asks which email was typed before anything else;
    admin-login.py --check ends with the name to sign in with and notes
    the sign-ins tried under an email no member has.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0000

maluos-office-setup (0.1.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The first sign-in can be checked and repaired: scripts/admin-login.py
    (--check: the administrator's member, the stored password against it,
    the sign-in throttle, the session cookie for the office's scheme, a real
    sign-in on the office; --reset: a new generated password, stored
    root-only, failed attempts cleared) and `maluctl office-setup admin
    [check|reset]`. The skill runs the check before handing the sign-in over
    and when the operator reports that it fails; verify.sh runs it too.
  * `claude` is found after the setup: `maluctl office-setup` adds
    ~/.local/bin to ~/.bashrc when the shell does not search it and says how
    to use it in the open shell; /etc/profile.d/maluos-local-bin.sh adds it
    for login shells. Before, `claude` typed after the setup answered
    "command not found" until the next login.
  * Local changes to the vendored plugin (to be carried to its repository):
    scripts/admin-login.py, scripts/verify.sh, skills/office-setup/SKILL.md,
    skills/office-check/SKILL.md, the troubleshooting reference.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 23:50:00 +0000

maluos-office-setup (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First version: the maluos-office-setup Claude Code plugin (skills
    office-setup, office-providers, office-check; the scripts preflight.py,
    configure-kernel.py, provision.sh, verify.sh, hosts-proxy.sh,
    proxy-config.sh, set-provider-key.sh, vm-guest.sh) vendored under
    /usr/share/maluos/claude-plugins with a local marketplace, the sudoers
    rule for its scripts, the launcher, and `maluctl office-setup`
    (run|check|status|providers). In seeds/business-os.seed, so every
    server image that carries the kernel carries the plugin that
    configures it (the handbook's 23-office-setup-package.md, phase 2).

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
